    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d948">

                <pb facs="0917" n="819" xml:id="pg819"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Merry to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">San José Costa Rica</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1900-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                                1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 454.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of my No. 115, dated July 28, addressed to Senor Don Dr. Fernando Sanchez,
                    minister of foreign affairs of the Republic of Nicaragua, written in relation to
                    the extraordinary action of Judge Roman at Bluefields in ignoring the agreement
                    of April 29, 1899, approved by both Governments, whereby the Bingham trust fund
                    was placed in the custody of Her Britannic Majesty’s consul at San Juan del
                    Norte, and its ultimate disposition referred to the foreign affairs departments
                    of both Governments.</p>
                <p>With assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Lawrence
                    Merry.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d948-a1.xml" xpointer="d948-a1"/>
